# Mutation plan for hijack.go (plugin plan Phase 3): crates/mm-plugin/src/hijack.rs.
#
#   MUTATE_PACKAGE=mm-plugin scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/mm-plugin-hijack.plan
#
# Every line filters to `hijack`: the unit tests in hijack::tests and the three rpc_http_*hijack*
# suites, whose Rust-with-Rust run exercises the same script both Go oracles do. Not planned: the
# size a plugin-side RW read asks for, which changes how many calls cross but not one byte the
# client sees; and `>=` made `>` in GoBufReader::read's bypass test, which survived its first run
# as an equivalent mutant: at p.len() == buf.len() the direct read and the fill ask for the same
# length and hand back the same bytes. CONTROL- lines must SURVIVE.
#
# First run, 2026-09-18: 13 run, 12 caught, the equivalent one above; both controls survived.

